    "result": "I couldn't run any checks after the fix, so it is untested. The sandbox blocked the inline `python -c` command. The earlier `pytest` run found no tests, so I didn't get a test run either.\n\nThe bug was in `_process_case` in `sqlparse/filters/reindent.py`. It took the first token of the CASE condition with `cond[1]`, but `cond` is a `(condition, value)` pair. Index 1 is the value list, which is empty for the first entry, so the call raised `IndexError: list index out of range`. I changed it to `cond[0]`, which is the condition tokens.\n\nThat is the change I expect to fix the two reindent case checks and the `compact` check. Please run the sqlparse tests, or a `sqlparse.format(..., reindent=True)` call on a CASE statement, to confirm."
  },
